[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
LumenShell needs a little system setup (groups, rc.conf, devfs rules,
wpa_supplicant control socket, syslog). Run, as root:

  /usr/local/share/lumenshell/freebsd/setup-system.sh -u <user>

or apply the samples in /usr/local/share/lumenshell/freebsd by hand:

  - pw groupmod video -m <user>; pw groupmod operator -m <user>
  - sysrc dbus_enable=YES seatd_enable=YES
  - /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf: ctrl_interface_group=wheel, update_config=1
  - devfs.rules, syslog.d and newsyslog.conf.d drop-ins

Then merge /usr/local/share/lumenshell/wayfire.ini.d/autostart.ini into
~/.config/wayfire.ini and start the session with start-lumenshell (or pick
"LumenShell" in your display manager).

lumen-lockscreen authenticates through the setuid-root helper
/usr/local/libexec/lumen-chkpass, because OpenPAM's pam_unix can only read
master.passwd as root. PAM policy: /usr/local/etc/pam.d/lumen-lockscreen.
EOM
}
]
